  "findings": [
    "Regex tier value: covers 76.2% of traffic at 83.8% accuracy for ~0 ms -> MARGINAL - review patterns; it wrongly fires on 1/25 chitchat rows (4.0%) and leaves 67 tool rows unmatched (worst: projects_query with 15 misses).",
    "Best operating point: strict (e2e@95% = 91.5%), auto-resolves 91.9% of traffic at 91.2% while escalating 8.1%; medium is the balanced default (92.9% auto at 91.0%, 7.1% escalated).",
    "Error concentration: 22 tier-0 errors vs 10 tier-1 errors; top confusions: timer_cancel->timer_create x7, shoppinglist_add->shoppinglist_view x6, shoppinglist_remove->shoppinglist_view x6.",
    "None-class leakage: regex FPs fire on 4.0% of chitchat; of chitchat reaching the router at medium, 4.2% of auto-handled chitchat leaks to a real tool (1/25 rows overall), 21 are safely escalated.",
    "Recommendation: keep the cascade at medium, add regex patterns for projects_query (largest regex miss bucket) and harden the timer_cancel->timer_create confusion (e.g. a negation/cancel disambiguator), then re-measure."
  ]
